  unmodified from https://github.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec (commit
  1742a253eb654bf8a4ed7c60eaef7412b2c23553), byte-identical to the published file at
  https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json.
  Copyright (c) OASIS Open 2023. All Rights Reserved. It is used only to validate Widedoor's
  SARIF output in tests. The OASIS notice that must accompany copies is in
  packages/report/vendor/sarif/LICENSE.md.

Docker seccomp profile
  docker/chromium-seccomp.json is the default seccomp profile of the Moby project
  (github.com/moby/profiles/seccomp v0.2.3, as vendored in https://github.com/moby/moby at tag
  docker-v29.6.1), Copyright 2013-2018 Docker, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
  Widedoor added one rule at the end (allowing clone, unshare and chroot) and reformatted it.

Docker image
  The image built from Dockerfile is not distributed by this repository. It contains, besides
  Widedoor: Node.js 24 on Debian bookworm (node:24.19.0-bookworm-slim), Chromium headless shell
  installed by Playwright 1.64.0 with the Debian packages it needs, a Java runtime made with
  jlink from Eclipse Temurin 11 (GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception), and veraPDF 1.30.3
  copied unmodified from verapdf/cli:v1.30.3 (dual licensed GPL-3.0-or-later or
  MPL-2.0-or-later, https://github.com/veraPDF/veraPDF-apps). Each keeps its own license.

Ajv, parse5
  The report tests use Ajv, ajv-draft-04 and ajv-formats (MIT) to validate the JSON and SARIF
  reports, and parse5 (MIT) to parse the HTML report. They are development dependencies only.
